# The corpus is compared byte for byte, and the round-trip promise is
# about bytes. Git normalising line endings on checkout would rewrite the
# fixtures before the tests ever saw them — on Windows the CRLF file and
# the LF files would both arrive as something else, and the failure would
# look like a bug in the parser.
crates/vuwr-core/tests/corpus/** -text
examples/** -text

# Everything else: normalise in the repository, check out with LF, so the
# sources do not acquire carriage returns on a Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf
